+# Data Model: Session End Host-Session Attribution Header
+
+**Feature**: [spec.md](spec.md) | **Date**: 2026-10-26
+
+No persistence schema changes are introduced by this feature. The entities below describe the
+runtime values the feature touches and how they relate; the only new element is one field on the
+end-of-session request entity.
+
+## Entity 1: Host Session Identifier
+
+| Property | Value |
+|----------|-------|
+| Name | `session` (in `_end_impl()`); wire source: hook payload key `session_id` |
+| Type | `str` |
+| Source | Host hook payload (`{"hook_event_name": "SessionEnd", "session_id": "..."}` read via `hook_input()`) |
+| Validation | `_session(payload)`: must be a string fully matching `ID = [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]{0,127}\Z`; if the environment variable `GRAPHHELM_SESSION_ID` is set, the payload value must also equal it. Any failure raises before HTTP traffic is sent. |
+| Length bound | 1..128 characters (from the grammar) |
+| Secrecy | Non-secret by construction: identifier grammar only; the same value already travels in today's `X-GraphHelm-Actor` composite and in state-file derivation. Token material never enters it. |
+| Uses after validation | Composite actor identity (`{host}-session-{session}`), local state path derivation, delivery receipt `sessionId`, **and (new)** the `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header value |
+
+**Constraints (from FR-002, FR-006):**
+- MUST equal the validated payload `session_id` — not the composite actor string, not the
+  execution identifier.
+- MUST NOT contain a host-name prefix (e.g. `claude-session-`), an execution identifier, or any
+  secret/token material.
+
+## Entity 2: End-of-Session Signal Request
+
+The HTTP request `_end_impl()` posts when a bound, not-yet-delivered session end occurs.
+**This feature adds exactly one field to this entity.**
+
+### Fields (unchanged)
+
+| Field | Location | Value | Change |
+|-------|----------|-------|--------|
+| Method | request | `POST` | unchanged |
+| Path | request | `/v1/executions/{execution}` with `execution` URL-quoted (`safe=''`) | unchanged |
+| Authorization | header | `Bearer {token}` from the token file | unchanged |
+| Content-Type | header | `application/json` (added by `request()` because a body is present) | unchanged |
+| Body `signal` | JSON | stored signal object built by `_signal()` (`id`, `source.type="tool"`, `source.id=<composite actor>`, `type="agent_session_ended"`, `severity`, `description`, `evidence=[execution]`, `emittedAt`) | unchanged |
+| `X-GraphHelm-Actor` | header | composite actor identity `{host}-session-{session}` | unchanged (FR-003) |
+| `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type` | header | `agent` | unchanged (FR-003) |
+| `Idempotency-Key` | header | `session-end-v2-<digest>` derived from `(execution, session, host, origin)` | unchanged (FR-003) |
+
+### Field (new)
+
+| Field | Location | Value | Rules |
+|-------|----------|-------|-------|
+| `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` | header (inline in the same dict as the other attribution headers) | The validated host session identifier (Entity 1) | FR-001/FR-002/FR-006; byte-for-byte identical across retries (SC-004); additive only (FR-003); end request only — absent from the start flow (FR-004) |
+
+Note: the *normative* header name is `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session`. Because Python 3.11's
+`urllib.request` title-cases outgoing header names, the bytes on the wire under the existing
+stdlib transport are `X-Graphhelm-Actor-Session`; HTTP consumers (including the Runtime) must
+treat the name case-insensitively, as with the existing actor headers (see
+[research.md R-4](research.md)).
+
+## Entity 3: Delivery Receipt (local hook state) — unchanged
+
+For reference of relationships only; schema stays at `version: 2`.
+
+| Field | Relation to this feature |
+|-------|--------------------------|
+| `sessionId` | Already equals the Entity 1 value; `_validate_delivery()` proves equality on every reload, which is what makes the new header retry-stable without storing anything new |
+| `signalId`, `signal`, `declaredNodeId`, `delivered` | Unchanged; no new persisted fields |
+| identity tuple (`executionId`, `host`, `origin`) | Unchanged scoping keys |
+
+## Relationships & flow
+
+```text
+hook payload.session_id
+        │  _session(): grammar + GRAPHHELM_SESSION_ID check (fail closed, pre-HTTP)
+        ▼
+   session ────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+        │                                                  │
+        ├──► composite actor "{host}-session-{session}"    │
+        │        │                                         │
+        │        ▼                                         ▼
+        │   X-GraphHelm-Actor header          X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session header  (NEW)
+        │                                                  ▲ byte-identical on retry:
+        ├──► signal body + Idempotency-Key                 │ _validate_delivery pins
+        └──► state path / receipt sessionId ───────────────┘ receipt sessionId == session
+```
+
+## State transitions
+
+Unchanged from current behavior:
+
+- First end event (bound, no receipt): receipt created with `delivered=false`, one POST sent.
+- Ack matches `(executionId, signalId)`: receipt updated `delivered=true`; later ends send nothing.
+- Refused/mismatched ack or transport failure: receipt unchanged (`delivered=false`); the next end
+  event resends the identical body, `Idempotency-Key`, and now the identical
+  `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` value.
+- Unbound end: no receipt, no request — no header involved.
+- Corrupt receipt: fail closed — no POST at all.
