+# Implementation Plan: Session End Host-Session Attribution Header
+
+**Branch**: `main` | **Date**: 2026-10-26 | **Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)
+
+**Input**: Feature specification from `/specs/001-bench/spec.md`
+
+**Provisioned-checkout notes** (recorded per task instructions):
+
+- No `.specify/extensions.yml` exists, so all extension hooks (`before_plan`, `after_plan`) are skipped; the `setup-plan` JSON was taken from Stage Setup.
+- No project constitution file exists in this checkout; the `AGENTS.md` file at the repository root is used as the governance reference in place of `/memory/constitution.md`.
+- The setup scripts under `.specify/scripts/` are not present in this checkout; the Stage Setup JSON is treated as their output.
+
+## Summary
+
+When a GraphHelm-bound agent session ends, `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py` posts an
+`agent_session_ended` signal to the Runtime but identifies only the composite actor
+(e.g. `claude-session-session-123`) in the `X-GraphHelm-Actor` header. This feature adds one
+attribution header — `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` — to that end-of-session POST, carrying the raw
+validated host session identifier from the hook payload. The change is strictly additive and
+inline (no new header helper), leaves every existing end-request header unchanged, does not touch
+the session-start request, and extends the existing end-request contract test to assert the new
+header's presence and exact value while keeping the whole hook test suite green.
+
+## Technical Context
+
+**Language/Version**: Python 3.11 (measured `Python 3.11.9` on this machine); the hook already
+uses `from __future__ import annotations` and stays stdlib-only.
+
+**Primary Dependencies**: None new. Existing stdlib modules only: `urllib.request`, `json`,
+`hashlib`, `re`, `argparse`, `tempfile`, `os`, `sys`, `subprocess`/`http.server` (tests).
+
+**Storage**: N/A for this change. The hook's local state file (JSON, 32 KiB bound) already persists
+the delivery receipt with `sessionId`; its schema is unchanged.
+
+**Testing**: Python `unittest` (`plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py`), which drives the
+hook through real subprocess calls against an in-process loopback `ThreadingHTTPServer` Runtime
+stub. No internet, Docker, credentials, provider accounts, or browser sessions.
+
+**Target Platform**: Windows PowerShell checkout (this machine); the hook must keep working on
+Windows, macOS, and Linux unchanged (existing `msvcrt`/`fcntl` branching untouched).
+
+**Project Type**: CLI lifecycle-hook script inside a plugin directory of an otherwise Rust
+workspace. Only two Python files in `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/` are in scope.
+
+**Performance Goals**: Unchanged. Hook HTTP timeout remains 1.0 s; input bound 64 KiB; reply
+bound 256 KiB.
+
+**Constraints**:
+
+- Additive only on the end POST: `X-GraphHelm-Actor`, `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type`, `Idempotency-Key`
+  stay present with unchanged values (FR-003).
+- No new reusable header-helper abstraction; the header is added inline to the end request (FR-005).
+- Session-start request must not gain the header and must otherwise be unchanged (FR-004).
+- Header value is the validated host session id only — no host-name prefix, execution id, or
+  secret/token material (FR-006).
+- Retried deliveries reuse the byte-for-byte identical value (SC-004).
+- All documentation stays in English (AGENTS.md documentation-language rule).
+
+**Scale/Scope**: One expression added to the inline header dict in `_end_impl` in
+`plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py` (line 349), plus assertions appended to the existing
+end-request test in `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py`
+(`test_end_posts_an_attributed_idempotent_observation_without_success_claim`).
+
+**Measured on-wire detail (see research.md)**: Python 3.11's `urllib.request` rewrites outgoing
+header names with `str.title()` in `AbstractHTTPHandler.do_request_`, so the stub server observes
+keys such as `X-Graphhelm-Actor`. The new header is therefore asserted in the stub as
+`X-Graphhelm-Actor-Session`; HTTP header case-insensitivity keeps the wire contract
+`X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` itself independent of that transport artifact.
+
+## Constitution Check
+
+*GATE: Must pass before Phase 0 research. Re-check after Phase 1 design.*
+
+Governance reference: `AGENTS.md` at the repository root (substituted for the absent project
+constitution file; see provisioned-checkout notes).
+
+| # | Gate (from AGENTS.md) | Result | Justification |
+|---|-----------------------|--------|---------------|
+| 1 | Documentation language: all docs in English | PASS | All artifacts in this feature directory are written in English. |
+| 2 | Smallest adequate observer; meaningful tests (Journey-Proven Development) | PASS | The promised behavior ("end request carries the host session id header") is observed directly by extending the existing contract test with presence + exact-value assertions against a real in-process stub — no proxy, no ceremony, no new test ritual. SC-001..SC-004 are each covered by an existing or extended test (see research.md). |
+| 3 | No scaffold/stub/TODO; minimal surface (FR-005 mirrors Keel "add only surface the promise needs") | PASS | One inline header entry in the existing request call; no new module, type, function, or helper. |
+| 4 | Security rules: secrets never appear in wire material | PASS | The value is the payload `session_id` after it has passed the strict identifier grammar `[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]{0,127}` (and, when configured, the `GRAPHHELM_SESSION_ID` equality check) in `_session()`; it is the same non-secret value already used to build the actor identity and key local state. Token material stays confined to `Authorization`. |
+| 5 | Tests run offline: no internet, Docker, credentials, or external infra | PASS | Reuses the existing in-process loopback `ThreadingHTTPServer` fixture and subprocess harness. |
+| 6 | Deterministic, bounded behavior; retries stable (append-only delivery semantics) | PASS | The header value derives from the validated payload session, which `_validate_delivery` already pins equal to the stored delivery `sessionId`; byte-for-byte stability across retries follows (SC-004, verified by the existing retry test pattern). |
+| 7 | Studio/CLI layering and crate boundaries (Rust workspace rules) | N/A | Change is confined to the Python plugin; no crate, schema, or wire-identifier migration touched. Provisional `p50.dev` identifiers untouched. |
+| 8 | No regression: previously passing tests stay green | PASS by design | Start flow code path (`_start_impl` briefing GET) is not modified; full-suite run in quickstart is the observer (SC-002, SC-003). |
+
+**Post-design re-evaluation (after Phase 1)**: re-checked against data-model.md and
+contracts/end-signal-request.md — no violation introduced; gate results unchanged. No
+complexity justification required.
+
