+# Quickstart: Validate Session End Host-Session Attribution Header
+
+**Feature**: [spec.md](spec.md) | **Date**: 2026-10-26
+
+Runnable validation that proves the feature works end-to-end from this checkout, using the hook's
+own in-process Runtime stub. No network, Docker, credentials, provider account, or browser session
+is required. The full test suite is the observer for both the new behavior (SC-001) and the
+no-regression promise (SC-002/SC-003); SC-004 is observed by the existing retry test which the
+implementation must extend.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- Python 3.11 (`python --version` → `3.11.x`). Only the standard library is used.
+- Run from the repository root so `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py` resolves relative to
+  its own directory (the test computes the script path from `__file__`).
+
+There is no build step and no setup command: the hook and its tests are plain Python files.
+
+## Validation 1 — End request carries the new header (SC-001, FR-001/FR-002/FR-006)
+
+Run only the end-request contract test:
+
+```powershell
+python plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py SessionHookTests.test_end_posts_an_attributed_idempotent_observation_without_success_claim
+```
+
+**Expected outcome**: exit code 0, `Ran 1 test`, `OK`. After implementation, this test must also
+assert — and pass — that the recorded end POST includes the header carrying the raw host session
+identifier. Under the stdlib client the stub records the key title-cased
+(`X-Graphhelm-Actor-Session`; see research.md R-4), with value exactly `session-123` (the value the
+test's payload supplies), while `X-Graphhelm-Actor` still equals the composite
+`claude-session-session-123`.
+
+Baseline before implementation (measured on this checkout): the same command already passes with
+the *old* assertions; the change extends the assertions.
+
+## Validation 2 — Retry reuses the identical header value (SC-004)
+
+The existing retry test is the observer once extended to compare the new header across attempts:
+
+```powershell
+python plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py SessionHookTests.test_failed_delivery_is_retryable_with_the_same_signal_bytes
+```
+
+**Expected outcome**: exit code 0, `OK`. It exercises a refused first delivery (`reply_ok=False`)
+followed by a successful retry and asserts byte-for-byte equality of the signal body and the
+`Idempotency-Key` across both POSTs; the implementation adds the same equality assertion for the
+`X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` value.
+
+## Validation 3 — Start flow unchanged and no regressions (SC-002, SC-003, FR-003/FR-004)
+
+Run the full hook suite:
+
+```powershell
+python plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py -v
+```
+
+**Expected outcome**: exit code 0, every test `ok`, a final `OK`. This covers:
+
+- Every pre-existing test continues to pass (no regressions — SC-002).
+- The start-flow tests (e.g. `test_bound_start_reads_live_briefing_but_does_not_promote_objective_to_instructions`)
+  keep passing unchanged, which — combined with the fact that the only edit is inside `_end_impl`'s
+  POST call — proves the start request gains no `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header (SC-003 / FR-004).
+- Secret-non-leakage assertions (`test-token`, objective text, `tool_input`) remain green.
+
+## What is NOT validated here (out of scope)
+
+- Building or exercising the Rust Runtime's acceptance of the new header — that is the consumer
+  side owned by the Runtime presence subsystem, not this hook-boundary feature. See the project's
+  normal Rust commands (`ci/gate.ps1` etc.) if a full workspace check is wanted; it is deliberately
+  not part of this feature's minimal observation.
+
+## Stop conditions
+
+- If any of the three commands above exits non-zero, stop and report it; do not treat a skipped or
+  unavailable observer as passing.
+- If the expected header cannot be observed because the stub does not record it (i.e. the transport
+  no longer emits the header), report `OBSERVER_MISSING` rather than inferring presence.
