+# Feature Specification: Session End Host-Session Attribution Header
+
+**Feature Branch**: `n/a` (branch creation is handled by the `before_specify` hook, which is skipped in this provisioned checkout; no `.specify/extensions.yml` exists)
+
+**Created**: 2026-10-26
+
+**Status**: Draft
+
+**Input**: User description: "When a GraphHelm-bound session ends, `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py` posts an `agent_session_ended` signal to the Runtime. The request names the actor (`X-GraphHelm-Actor`) but not the host session, so the Runtime's structured presence record has no session id. Send the host session id in the `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header of that end request, and extend the existing end-request test in `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py` to assert it. Do not add a new header helper or change the start request; the hook's other tests must stay green."
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing *(mandatory)*
+
+### User Story 1 - Attribute an ended session to its host session (Priority: P1)
+
+When a GraphHelm-bound agent session ends, the hook posts an `agent_session_ended` signal to the Runtime. Today the request identifies the *actor* (a composite of host and session, e.g. `claude-session-session-123`) but not the raw host session identifier on its own, so the Runtime's structured presence record cannot record which originating host session produced the observation. After this feature, every end-of-session signal request carries the host session identifier in a dedicated `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header, so the Runtime can attribute the presence record to the exact originating session without having to reverse-engineer it from the composite actor name.
+
+**Why this priority**: This is the core value of the feature. Without it the Runtime's presence record remains ambiguous about the originating session; with it, presence accounting is directly attributable per session. It is the minimal slice that delivers the complete user need on its own.
+
+**Independent Test**: Fully testable by running the existing end-of-session contract test against the in-process Runtime stub and asserting that the recorded end request contains the `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header carrying the host session identifier. That single assertion delivers the observable outcome.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+
+1. **Given** a bound session (an execution binding is configured) whose host payload carries a valid host session identifier, **When** the hook handles the session-end event and posts the `agent_session_ended` signal, **Then** the request sent to the Runtime includes the `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header whose value equals that host session identifier.
+2. **Given** the same end request described above, **When** it is posted, **Then** all headers the request carried before this change (actor identity, actor type, idempotency key) are still present with unchanged values, and the new header is additive only.
+3. **Given** the existing contract test for the end request, **When** the test suite runs, **Then** it asserts the new header's presence and value and passes, and every other hook test in the suite continues to pass.
+
+---
+
+### User Story 2 - Keep the session-start flow unchanged (Priority: P2)
+
+The new header belongs specifically to the end-of-session signal request. The session-start flow already behaves correctly and must not gain a new header or otherwise change as a side effect of this work.
+
+**Why this priority**: Protects against regression. The value delivered by Story 1 is only trustworthy if the rest of the hook's observable behavior is provably unchanged.
+
+**Independent Test**: Testable by running the session-start contract tests and confirming the start request's header set is exactly what it was before the change (no `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header appears on the start request).
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+
+1. **Given** a bound session at start time, **When** the hook handles the session-start event, **Then** the briefing request it sends does not include the `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header.
+2. **Given** the full hook test suite before and after the change, **When** both are run, **Then** no previously passing test changes result (the change introduces no regressions).
+
+---
+
+### Edge Cases
+
+- **Unbound end (no execution configured):** No request is sent to the Runtime at all, so there is nothing to attach a header to. Behavior and silence are unchanged from today.
+- **Retry after a refused or mismatched acknowledgment:** Delivery is retried using the same stored signal. The retried end request MUST reuse the identical `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` value as the original attempt, consistent with how the signal body and idempotency key already stay stable across retries.
+- **Declared node binding present:** A configured node label affects only the descriptive text of the signal. The `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header still carries only the raw host session identifier and is not affected by node binding.
+- **Header value source:** The value sent MUST be the validated host session identifier taken from the host payload, not the composite actor string and not the execution identifier. It MUST NOT contain secret or token material.
+
+## Requirements *(mandatory)*
+
+### Functional Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: The system MUST include the host session identifier in the end-of-session signal request sent to the Runtime, transmitted in the `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header.
+- **FR-002**: The value of `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` MUST equal the validated host session identifier supplied by the host hook payload — the same identifier the hook already uses to build the actor identity and to scope local hook state.
+- **FR-003**: The change MUST be additive on the end request: every header the end request carried before the change (actor identity, actor type, idempotency key) MUST remain present with unchanged values.
+- **FR-004**: The session-start request MUST NOT gain the `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header, and the start flow MUST otherwise be unchanged.
+- **FR-005**: No new reusable header-helper abstraction MAY be introduced for this change; the header is added inline to the end request.
+- **FR-006**: The `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` value MUST be the raw host session identifier only — it MUST NOT include the host-name prefix (e.g. `claude-session-`), the execution identifier, or any secret/token material.
+- **FR-007**: The existing end-request contract test MUST be extended to assert the presence and value of the `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header on the posted end request, and the extension MUST pass while leaving all other hook tests green.
+
+### Key Entities
+
+- **End-of-session signal request**: The HTTP request the hook sends to the Runtime when a bound session ends. It carries the signal body plus attribution headers (actor identity, actor type, idempotency key). This feature adds one more attribution header (`X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session`) to it.
+- **Host session identifier**: The session identifier the host supplies in the end-of-session payload and that the hook validates against its identifier grammar. It is the single source of the new header's value and is distinct from both the composite actor identity and the execution identifier.
+
+## Success Criteria *(mandatory)*
+
+### Measurable Outcomes
+
+- **SC-001**: 100% of bound end-of-session signal requests observed by the Runtime carry a non-empty `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header whose value equals the originating host session identifier.
+- **SC-002**: In the end-request contract test, the new header's presence and exact value are asserted and pass, and zero previously passing hook tests regress (the full hook suite stays green).
+- **SC-003**: Zero new headers appear on the session-start request relative to the pre-change behavior.
+- **SC-004**: For any retried end-of-session delivery, the `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` value is byte-for-byte identical across attempts (idempotent), matching the stability already required of the signal body and idempotency key.
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- **Host session identifier = the validated `session_id` from the host hook payload.** This is the identifier the hook already validates and uses for the actor and state keying; it is bounded by the existing identifier grammar and contains no secrets.
+- **The wire identifier `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` is the agreed header name shared with the Runtime presence subsystem.** The header name is treated here as part of the wire contract that makes the outcome verifiable (it is what the contract test asserts), even though the surrounding behavior is described technology-agnostically.
+- **Provisioned-checkout substitutions:** No `.specify/extensions.yml` exists, so both `before_specify` and `after_specify` hooks are skipped, and branch creation did not occur. No project constitution file exists in this checkout; `AGENTS.md` at the repository root is used as the governance reference in its place.
+- **Scope is strictly bounded to the end request** of `session_hook.py` and its end-request contract test. The start request, the signal body contents, the idempotency scheme, and local state schema are out of scope and must remain unchanged.
